WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.690
Great movies are like a conversation.

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:08.480
Filmmakers are communicating with the audience,
sure—but they're also communicating with

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.310
each other...or sometimes themselves.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:17.010
Often, directors just can't help themselves,
and let everyone eavesdrop on their cinematic

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.330
conversations.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:22.769
Here are hidden Easter eggs that reference
other movies.

00:00:22.769 --> 00:00:24.099
Toy Story

00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:29.710
While trapped at Sid's house, Buzz Lightyear
experiences a small existential crisis and

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:30.930
starts wandering.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.440
Does that carpet seem familiar?

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.020
That's because it was lifted from the Overlook
Hotel in The Shining.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:44.360
While we appreciate the nod to a Stanley Kubrick
classic, we're happy Pixar stopped short of

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:49.280
showing us creepy twins or elevators full
of blood.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.690
Zootopia

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:56.190
Toward the end of Zootopia, Duke Weaselton
is selling bootleg DVDs on the street.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:01:01.760
In addition to the fact that Duke Weaselton’s
name is a reference to Frozen's Duke of Weselton...

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:08.619
...the DVDs he's selling are animal versions
of Disney films like Big Hero 6, Tangled,

00:01:08.619 --> 00:01:10.549
Wreck-It Ralph, and more.

00:01:10.549 --> 00:01:13.500
Does anyone else really want to actually see
these movies?

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:19.499
Considering Pig Hero 6 is billed as "the best
animated movie on this DVD," it's gotta be

00:01:19.499 --> 00:01:20.740
good, right?

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.679
Captain America: The Winter Soldier

00:01:23.679 --> 00:01:29.270
Captain America: The Winter Soldier boasts
some super-spy action featuring Nick Fury,

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:31.710
played by Samuel L. Jackson.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:37.299
He's probably still most famous for his role
in Pulp Fiction as Jules Winnfield.

00:01:37.299 --> 00:01:41.310
Jules quoted a Bible verse right before gunning
down a man .

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:45.540
"Ezekiel 25:17?

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:52.049
The path of the righteous man is beset on
all sides by the inequities of the selfish,

00:01:52.049 --> 00:01:54.159
and the tyranny of evil men."

00:01:54.159 --> 00:02:00.789
Part of that same quote is on Fury's headstone
after he’s presumed dead.

00:02:00.789 --> 00:02:01.799
Rango

00:02:01.799 --> 00:02:06.929
In this Johnny Depp film, Rango gets into
some trouble and tumbles around on the highway

00:02:06.929 --> 00:02:08.259
in the desert.

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:14.420
Before he gets to safety, Rango ends up pancaked
on the windshield of a Cadillac Eldorado...being

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:19.990
driven by the characters from Fear and Loathing
in Las Vegas, starring Johnny Depp.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:26.080
The kids must’ve gotten a kick out of this,
because children just love Hunter S. Thompson.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.670
Coming to America

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:33.420
Coming to America stars Eddie Murphy as a
young African prince intent on experiencing

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.600
what America has to offer.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:41.390
During his travels, he encounters some down-on-their-luck
brothers who could use a buck or two.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:47.250
These bums just happen to be the Duke Brothers,
the antagonists from Murphy's earlier hit,

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.250
Trading Places.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:54.340
After going broke in the previous movie, it's
nice to see Prince Akeem lending a hand.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.150
Charlie and the Chocolate Factory

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:00.640
In Tim Burton's Charlie and the Chocolate
Factory, we find out that Charlie's dad makes

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:05.840
very little money screwing on the caps of
Smilex toothpaste at a factory.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:09.430
But did you realize that we've heard of Smilex
before?

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:12.640
Way back in Tim Burton's Batman from 1989:

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.940
"New and improved Joker products!

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:20.990
With a new secret ingredient, Smilex!"

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:23.020
The Polar Express

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:29.260
Robert Zemeckis directed The Polar Express,
a CGI Christmas movie starring Tom Hanks.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:34.160
He also directed the Back to the Future series,
featuring one of the most iconic time machines

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:36.350
ever: the DeLorean.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:38.860
Remember what makes the DeLorean work?

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.950
That's right, the Flux Capacitor.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:48.070
Well, it turns out that’s how the Polar
Express gets to the North Pole so fast.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:49.140
Predator 2

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:54.380
While watching Predator 2, you can spot a
skull in the trophy room that looks pretty

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.470
familiar.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:04:01.600
In case you were wondering, yes, it does belong
to a Xenomorph from the Alien movies—and

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:07.290
its presence is only natural because Aliens
and Predators live in a shared universe.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:11.371
And it's always hunting season for the Predators.

00:04:11.371 --> 00:04:18.430
Still, they better hope they never try to
hunt rabbits.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:19.430
Thanks for watching!

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:23.639
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:23.639 --> 00:04:28.400
And leave us a comment to let us know which
Easter egg was the biggest surprise to you.

